WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.925
Your cloud decides what you can use,
and this picture changes monthly.

2
00:00:03.925 --> 00:00:06.175
The platform is generally available.

3
00:00:06.175 --> 00:00:10.846
GCC has a documented subset: you can
govern agent identity and access,

4
00:00:10.846 --> 00:00:15.763
but not yet get Microsoft's audit and
data protection for agent activity.

5
00:00:15.763 --> 00:00:20.075
GCC High and DoD have nothing
published, so treat agent identities

6
00:00:20.075 --> 00:00:24.074
as unavailable there until
Microsoft confirms it in writing.

7
00:00:24.074 --> 00:00:29.013
Licensing is its own trap, and the FedRAMP
High authorization is still pending.

8
00:00:29.013 --> 00:00:33.467
The program's rule is to build on what's
generally available in your own cloud,

9
00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:36.012
and to treat preview as
something you watch.

10
00:00:36.012 --> 00:00:38.040
So how do we classify all this?
